# npm audit policy: fail on critical only (audit-level sets the exit code, not what
# `npm audit` reports). Re-check on every aws-cdk-lib upgrade and remove this file once
# the finding below clears.
#
# As of aws-cdk-lib 2.277.0 and aws-cdk 2.1148.1 (the latest releases) `npm audit`
# reports 2 moderate findings from one root cause:
#
# - GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (CVE-2026-118764): minimatch <11.0.1, DoS through glob pattern
#   amplification. The vulnerable copy (10.2.6) is bundled inside aws-cdk-lib, and npm
#   overrides do not apply to bundled dependencies. The minimatch and glob overrides in
#   package.json clear the copies in the Jest tree only. aws/aws-cdk PR #39595 bumps the
#   bundled copy to 11.0.8. It merged on 2026-11-13, after 2.277.0 was cut, so no release
#   contains it yet. CDK uses minimatch at synth time on this repository's own paths, not
#   on untrusted patterns.
#
# Do not run "npm audit fix --force": it proposes downgrading aws-cdk-lib to 2.239.0.
audit-level=critical
